  <div class="lh-container">
    
<header class="main-header">
  <div class="series-title">Likutay Halachos · Choshen Mishpat</div>
  <h1>Hilchos Aidus 5 — Part 1</h1>
  <div class="subtitle">Laws of Testimony — 5 (Osiyos 1–9)</div>
</header>
<div class="verse-block">
  <span class="scripture">"Testimony requires no fewer than two, as it is written: 'By the mouth of two witnesses or by the mouth of three witnesses a matter shall be established'"</span>
  <span class="source-ref">Based on the Torah "Ki Saitzai LaMilchamah" — Likutay Moharan II, at the end, Siman 82; see there from beginning to end</span>
</div>
<div class="os-header">Os 1</div>
<p>Based on the Torah <span class="scripture">"Ki Saitzai LaMilchamah"</span> [When you go out to war] in Likutay Tinyana at its end, Siman 82; see there from beginning to end. And the general principle is that one must include the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> <span class="key-term-def">[not in order]</span> within the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span> <span class="key-term-def">[in order]</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">mah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[what — i.e. self-nullification]</span>, from where the essential life-force derives, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">"what are our lives, what is our strength"</span> etc. And when a person sees that things are going for him <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>, he should know that he has <span class="key-term">gadlus</span> <span class="key-term-def">[inflated ego]</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="aramaic">"I shall reign"</span> <span class="key-term-def">[ana emloch]</span>, which separates the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> [kingship] for himself etc. Therefore he should do <span class="key-term">t'shuvah</span> and humble himself and be in the aspect of <span class="key-term">mah</span> etc.</p>
<p>And the essential <span class="key-term">t'shuvah</span> is accomplished in the month of Elul, when Moshe made a <span class="key-term">derech k'vushah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[a beaten path]</span> to travel upon — a path of <span class="key-term">t'shuvah</span>. And the path of <span class="key-term">t'shuvah</span> that Moshe made in Elul was through binding himself with all the levels and revealing and making known that Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> is in every place, in all the levels that exist in the world, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">"If I ascend to the heavens, You are there; if I make my bed in the abyss, behold, You are there"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 139:8)</span>. For even in the <span class="aramaic">eser kisrin d'mesaavusa</span> <span class="key-term-def">[ten crowns of impurity]</span>, even there Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> is found, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">"and His sovereignty rules over all"</span> etc. And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">chirik</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the lower vowel-point]</span>, in the aspect of <span class="aramaic">"and through the chirik, to reign over the lower ones"</span> etc. And likewise in every ascent upon ascent, he found Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> there. For sometimes, from the abundance of good that is given to a person, he becomes distant etc. But Moshe Rabbeinu revealed that even there Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> is found etc. And this is the aspect of the <span class="key-term">segol</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the upper vowel-point]</span> etc.; see all of this there well.</p>
<div class="os-header">Os 2</div>
<p>And this is the aspect of testimony through two, and <span class="aramaic">"two are like a hundred"</span> [tray k'me'ah]. For the witnesses come to reveal the truth, and the essential truth is through the aforementioned aspect — through nullifying oneself in the aspect of <span class="key-term">mah</span>, until <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> is included in <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>. For falsehood, which is the opposite of truth, has its essential hold from the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>. For truth is the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>, and falsehood is the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>. For truth is when one says about each thing as it is — for instance, about silver, "silver," and about copper, "copper" etc. — which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>, that one states the truth according to the order of Creation of these things. But falsehood is the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>, that one wishes to change the order of Creation and says about silver that it is copper, or the reverse. And likewise every falsehood that one speaks — it is all the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>, that he changes the true order of that object or matter and states it not according to the order of the event that occurred.</p>
<p>It emerges that falsehood is the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>. And therefore the essential nullification of falsehood is through the aspect of the path of <span class="key-term">t'shuvah</span> that Moshe made in Elul — which is to include the lower point in the upper point, through which <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> is included in <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span> etc., as above. For this is the essential completeness of truth: when the truth is complete from beginning to end, from the peak of all levels to the end of all levels. For <span class="key-term">emes</span> [truth] is beginning, middle, and end, as is brought: for the <em>alef</em> is the first of all the letters, and the <em>tav</em> is the last of all the letters, and the <em>mem</em> is in the middle, as is brought. That is, the essential truth is when it is truth from beginning to end, as above.</p>
<p>For the <em>alef</em>, which is the first of all the letters — this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">alef-bais</span>, <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>. And the <em>tav</em>, which is the last of all the letters — this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tav-shin-reish-kuf</span>, <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>, as is written at the beginning of the aforementioned Torah: that the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">alef-bais</span>, and the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tav-shin-reish-kuf</span> [i.e. the reverse alphabet]. That is, the <em>alef</em> of <span class="key-term">emes</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">alef-bais ka'seder</span>, the aspect of the upper point. And the <em>tav</em> of <span class="key-term">emes</span> — this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tav-shin-reish-kuf shelo ka'seder</span>, the aspect of the lower point. And the <em>mem</em> of <span class="key-term">emes</span>, which is in the middle — this is the aspect of that which connects and includes the lower point in the upper point, to include <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> in <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>. And this is the essential completeness and life-force and rectification of all Creation, as is understood from the aforementioned Torah.</p>
<p>For the <em>mem</em> is the aspect of the forty days from Rosh Chodesh Elul until Yom HaKippurim. In these forty days Moshe ascended on high and made the beaten path for the aforementioned <span class="key-term">t'shuvah</span> — which is to include the lower point in the upper point, to include <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> in <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>, to include the <em>tav</em> — the aspect of the end, the aspect of <span class="key-term">tav-shin-reish-kuf shelo ka'seder</span> — in the aspect of the <em>alef</em>, which is the beginning, the aspect of <span class="key-term">alef-bais ka'seder</span>. So that everything is included together through the <em>mem</em> that is in the middle, and then the aspect of <span class="key-term">emes</span> [truth] is completed — which is the essential rectification of the world. For with it the Holy One, Blessed be He, sealed His world, as it is written: <span class="scripture">"B'reishis bara Elokim"</span> — the final letters spell <span class="key-term">emes</span>, as is brought. For the essential truth is when it is truth from beginning to end: that in every level in the world one finds Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, Who is truth itself — whether in ascent or in descent — and one does not overturn the truth <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>, whether on account of the ascent or on account of the descent.</p>
<p>For sometimes a person, on account of his ascent — in wealth, or in wisdom, being an outstanding scholar of Torah — through this turns from the truth and overturns it from its true order, and disputes true tzadikim and G-d-fearing people, because he says arguments that are the opposite of the actual truth. For there is no end to the empty words one can say about anything to overturn it from the truth, and it is impossible to explain and refute all the errors and all the reverse arguments. Rather, the truth testifies for itself, and whoever has a Jewish heart and nullifies himself in the aspect of <span class="key-term">mah</span> and desires the actual truth and does not wish to deceive himself — he can know and understand the truth well.</p>
<p>And likewise, sometimes on account of a great descent — that he fell and descended into the exile of desires greatly, each person according to his descent — until on account of this his spirits fall, as if hope is lost, until the <span class="key-term">Ba'al Davar</span> [Adversary] wants to make him despair of mercy, <em>chas v'sholom</em>, and it seems to him that in truth his hope has already been lost, <em>chas v'sholom</em>. And all of this is because he overturns the truth <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>. For in truth, the actual truth is not so. For Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> has already revealed to us His abundant mercies that do not cease, through Moshe Rabbeinu and through the true tzadikim who followed him, who revealed that Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> is in every place — as is explained in this Torah: that Moshe Rabbeinu revealed that even in the <span class="aramaic">eser kisrin d'mesaavusa</span>, which is the totality of all the impurities in the world, <em>Rachmana litzlan</em>, even there Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> is found, as above. Therefore the essential completeness of truth is when it is truth in every level, from beginning to end, as above.</p>
<div class="os-header">Os 3</div>
<p>It emerges that the essential truth is when the lower point is included in the upper point etc., as above. And this is the aspect of two testimonies. For when two align their testimony, this is the aspect of the two points being included together. For wherever there are two of Yisroel, the aspect of the two aforementioned points shines in them. For certainly no two people are equal, and certainly one is greater than the other — as is written in the Mishnah regarding two witnesses: "They bring in the greater one first" etc. (and as is brought above on this topic). And wherever there is a greater and a lesser, they are drawn in their root from the aspect of the two aforementioned points, which are the upper point and the lower point.</p>
<p>And when these two are included together and state their testimony equally, the Torah trusts them like a hundred. For certainly their words are truth, since the essential truth comes only through this — through the two points being included together. And this is the aspect of two witnesses who align their words: both of them say the same thing, which is the aspect of the two points being included together — and this is the essential truth, as above.</p>
<div class="os-header">Os 4</div>
<p>And this is: <span class="scripture">"By the mouth of two witnesses etc., a matter [<em>davar</em>] shall be established [<em>yakum</em>]"</span> — <span class="precise">"yakum davar," specifically</span>. For <span class="key-term">davar</span> [word/matter] is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, the aspect of Chavah, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">dibur</span> [speech], which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus Peh</span> <span class="key-term-def">[Kingship = the Mouth]</span>. From there the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> is drawn when one separates, <em>chas v'sholom</em>, the <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> for oneself, as is written there.</p>
<p>And the essential rectification is to raise and establish the <span class="key-term">dibur</span> — the aspect of Chavah, the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> — to its root, to the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>. And this is accomplished through the two witnesses who testify truthful testimony, as above. And this is: <span class="scripture">"By the mouth of two witnesses etc., <em>yakum davar</em>"</span> — that they establish and raise the aspect of <span class="key-term">davar</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus Peh</span>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>, to its root, to the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span> — through revealing the truth between the litigants, as above.</p>
<div class="os-header">Os 5</div>
<p>And this is the aspect of the great virtue of peace and the repugnance of <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> [dispute], as our Sages, of blessed memory, said: <span class="aramaic">"Dispute is despised, and peace is great."</span> For the more that several people of Yisroel are included together in peace and love, the more the aforementioned points are included together, and the more <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> is included in <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span> — which is the essential rectification of all the worlds, which were created for this purpose, as is understood by the discerning from the aforementioned Torah.</p>
<p>And therefore Moshe Rabbeinu, each time there was <span class="key-term">machlokes</span> against him and against Aharon, said: <span class="scripture">"And we — what [<em>mah</em>] are we?"</span> <span class="source">(Exodus 16:7)</span>. And likewise: <span class="scripture">"And Aharon — what is he, that you complain against him?"</span> <span class="source">(Numbers 16:11)</span>. For the essential rectification is through the aspect of <span class="key-term">mah</span>. For all those who dispute and fight against him are from the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>, who wish to overturn the truth from its true order, as above. And therefore the rectification for this is the aspect of <span class="key-term">mah</span>: one must nullify oneself in the aspect of <span class="key-term">mah</span>, and through this everything will be included in the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>, and the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> will be nullified, as above. And through this all the enemies and disputants who draw sustenance from there — from the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> — will fall and be nullified. For everything is nullified through the aspect of <span class="key-term">mah</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>, as above.</p>
<div class="os-header">Os 6</div>
<p>And this is the aspect of the immersion of the <span class="key-term">mikveh</span>. For all impurities are drawn from the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">dinim</span> [judgments], from where the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achara</span> draws sustenance, and from where all impurities derive. And when one wishes to purify oneself, one must nullify oneself in the aspect of <span class="key-term">mah</span> and be included in the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>. And this is through the immersion of the <span class="key-term">mikveh</span>. For the measure of forty <span class="key-term">se'ah</span> corresponds to the forty days in which Moshe ascended and made the beaten path for the aforementioned <span class="key-term">t'shuvah</span>, through which everything is included in the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>.</p>
<p>And therefore, through entering the waters of the <span class="key-term">mikveh</span> of forty <span class="key-term">se'ah</span> — the aspect of the aforementioned <em>mem</em> [forty] — and being concealed and covered there within the water and being nullified there, through this one is included in the aspect of <span class="key-term">mah</span>, in the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>. Through this all the impurities that are drawn from the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> are nullified, and one ascends from impurity to purity, for one is included in the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>, as above. And see in the <span class="key-term">Kavanos</span> [mystical intentions of the Arizal], where it is explained that the forty <span class="key-term">se'ah</span> of the <span class="key-term">mikveh</span> correspond to the forty days that Moshe ascended.</p>
<div class="os-header">Os 7</div>
<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="scripture">"And I call to witness against them the heavens and the earth"</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 4:26)</span>. For heaven and earth are the aspect of the upper point and the lower point, which are the aspect of two witnesses, as above. And in it is the matter of Rosh HaShanah.</p>
<div class="os-header">Os 8</div>
<p>And this is the aspect of Rosh HaShanah and Yom HaKippurim, which are the Ten Days of Repentance, corresponding to the aspect of the <em>yud</em> mentioned above, which is made through including <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> in <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>, as is explained there in the aforementioned Torah. For on Rosh HaShanah the world was created, and the entire world was created only in order to reveal <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> through the person.</p>
<p>And therefore the entire service on Rosh HaShanah is to include <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> in <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span> — which is the aspect of the sweetening of the judgments that one is occupied with most on Rosh HaShanah, which is the Day of Judgment. For all the judgments are from the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">dinim</span>. For the general Creation of the world is in the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> relative to Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, in the aspect of <span class="aramaic">"In Tishrei the world was created"</span> <span class="source">(Rosh HaShanah 10b)</span>. <span class="key-term">Tishrei</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">tav-shin-reish-kuf</span> — <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>. For certainly the physicality of the world is the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> relative to His Wisdom, <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Chochmah</span> — <span class="key-term">koach mah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[the power of "what"]</span>. For certainly physicality is the opposite — that is, the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> relative to the aspect of <span class="key-term">mah</span>.</p>
<p>But in truth, these are His mighty acts and awesome deeds — that He created something from absolute nothingness. And it was all in order to reveal His sovereignty. Through this, <span class="precise">specifically</span> — through the person believing in the truth and nullifying himself, together with the entire world that depends upon him, in the aspect of <span class="key-term">mah</span>, and constantly connecting His G-dliness in his thought in the aspect of <span class="aramaic">chashov — mah</span> <span class="key-term-def">[think — what]</span>, as is written there at the end of the aforementioned Torah — through this one returns the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>, which is the aspect of the totality of the world, to be included in the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>. And this is the essential completeness and fulfillment and sustaining of the world, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">"To Hashem is the earth and its fullness"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 24:1)</span>, as is written there.</p>
<p>And this is all our service on Rosh HaShanah, when the world was created — which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>, as above, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">dinim</span>, as above. For then we are occupied with publicizing His sovereignty, which rules over all — that is, that the entire world, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>, is entirely included in Him, <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, which is the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>. For we do not separate, <em>chas v'sholom</em>, the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> for ourselves, Heaven forbid. Rather, we acknowledge and make known that <span class="scripture">"His sovereignty rules over all"</span> — that He, <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, reigns and rules over all, from the height of all levels to the end of all levels, to the very lowest level. For even in the <span class="aramaic">eser kisrin d'mesaavusa</span>, His sovereignty rules, <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>.</p>
<p>And therefore we say in all the blessings on Rosh HaShanah: "King over all the earth" etc. And likewise: "Reign over the entire world in its totality" etc. For this is the essential service of Rosh HaShanah — to reveal His sovereignty, which rules over all, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">"To Hashem is the earth and its fullness,"</span> which we say at the entrance of Rosh HaShanah. For through this, the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> — which is the totality of the world — returns to be included in the aspect of <span class="key-term">ka'seder</span>. And through this is the essential sweetening of the judgments that are held in the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span>, as above.</p>
<div class="os-header">Os 9</div>
<p>And this is the aspect of: <span class="scripture">"I call to witness against you today the heavens and the earth"</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 30:19)</span>, [the portion] that we always read close to Rosh HaShanah. For <span class="precise">specifically</span> two witnesses are needed to reveal the truth from amidst the falsehood, and they are the aspect of heaven and earth — which is the aspect of above and below, the lower point and the upper point, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">"If I ascend to the heavens, You are there; and if I make my bed in the abyss, behold, You are there."</span></p>
<p>For the totality of the Torah is <span class="key-term">emunah</span> [faith], as it is written: <span class="scripture">"All Your mitzvos are faith"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 119:86)</span>. And as our Sages, of blessed memory, said: <span class="aramaic">"Chavakuk came and established them upon one — which is faith"</span> <span class="source">(Makkos 24a)</span>. And the essential <span class="key-term">emunah</span>, which depends upon truth, as is written elsewhere — is in the two aforementioned aspects. That is, one must believe in Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, that He is the Singular Primordial One — He was, He is, and He will be. And just as one must believe in His existence, <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, so too one must believe that He is the Creator, the Former, the Governor — King, Ruler, and Sovereign — and He oversees everything from beginning to end. For when one does not believe, <em>chas v'sholom</em>, that He, <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, rules over all perpetually and that <span class="scripture">"His sovereignty rules over all,"</span> he is a denier who <span class="aramaic">"cuts the plantings."</span></p>
<p>And therefore the essential <span class="key-term">emunah</span> is in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">"And you shall know today and return it to your heart, that Hashem is G-d in the heavens above and upon the earth below — there is nothing else"</span> <span class="source">(Deuteronomy 4:39)</span>. For one must crown Him above and below, in the heavens above and upon the earth below, to believe that <span class="scripture">"His sovereignty rules over all."</span> And this itself is the aspect of <span class="scripture">"Hashem is G-d"</span> [Hashem hu HaElokim] — for <span class="key-term">Hashem</span> [the Tetragrammaton] is the aspect of <span class="key-term">mah</span>, for <span class="key-term">Havayah</span> filled with <em>alefs</em> is numerically <span class="key-term">mah</span>, as above. And <span class="key-term">Elokim</span> is the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span>, as it is written: <span class="scripture">"And G-d is my King from of old"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 74:12)</span>. That is, to unify the aspect of <span class="key-term">Malchus</span> — the aspect of <span class="key-term">shelo ka'seder</span> — in the aspect of <span class="key-term">mah</span>, through knowing and believing that <span class="scripture">"His sovereignty rules over all,"</span> as above.</p>
<p>And therefore the entire Torah is called <span class="key-term">aidus</span> [testimony], as it is written: <span class="scripture">"And He established a testimony in Yaakov"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 78:5)</span>. The aspect of the two <span class="key-term">Luchos HaAidus</span> [Tablets of Testimony] — <span class="precise">"two," specifically</span>, for <span class="precise">specifically</span> two witnesses are needed, as above. And therefore the two <span class="key-term">Luchos HaAidus</span> were given on Yom HaKippurim, which is the completion of the aforementioned forty days, in which Moshe ascended and made the beaten path for <span class="key-term">t'shuvah</span> — which is in the two aforementioned aspects, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">"If I ascend to the heavens, You are there; and if I make my bed in the abyss, behold, You are there"</span> — which are the aspect of two witnesses, the aspect of heaven and earth, above and below, who reveal the truth, which is the aspect of beginning, middle, and end.</p>
<p>For this is the essential <span class="key-term">t'shuvah</span>: when one knows and believes that Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> is found with him always, at every time and in every place where he is, as it is written: <span class="scripture">"In all the places of His dominion"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 103:22)</span>. And through this he will merit to travel upon the path of <span class="key-term">t'shuvah</span> that Moshe made.</p>
<p>For the essential power of the <span class="key-term">yetzer hara</span> and the <span class="key-term">Sitra Achara</span> — all their power comes through the falsehood, which is the evil, which is the impurity, as is written in the Torah <span class="scripture">"Amar Rabbi Akiva"</span> <span class="source">(Siman 51)</span>. For first it causes the person to sin through its lies, misleading him through many types of deceptions. And afterward, when it comes to his mind to return, it weakens his resolve and implants in his heart that Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> has already departed from him, and he is so distant that it is impossible for him to return. But in truth it is the opposite — for in truth <span class="scripture">"His sovereignty rules over all,"</span> even in the <span class="aramaic">eser kisrin d'mesaavusa</span>. And as it is written: <span class="scripture">"Who dwells with them amidst their impurities"</span> <span class="source">(Leviticus 16:16)</span>. And as Rashi explains: even when they are impure, the <span class="key-term">Sh'chinah</span> is with them.</p>
<p>And therefore one must know that this is the essential path of <span class="key-term">t'shuvah</span> that Moshe made in Elul. And the true tzadikim and those who follow them draw this path in every single year. And the essential thing is that they know and make known, in many languages and warnings and proclamations without number, that Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span> is still with us — with each and every one, even with the worst sinner in the entire world. For <span class="scripture">"His sovereignty rules over all,"</span> in the aspect of <span class="scripture">"and if I make my bed in the abyss, behold, You are there."</span></p>
<p>And as long as a person turns this over in his mind and heart and truly implants this in his heart, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">"And you shall know today and return it to your heart, that Hashem is G-d in the heavens above and upon the earth below"</span> etc., as above — then certainly he has great hope all the days of his life to merit the path of <span class="key-term">t'shuvah</span> in truth. For this is the essential path of <span class="key-term">t'shuvah</span> that Moshe and the tzadikim who followed him made, as above, in the aspect of: <span class="scripture">"Who makes a path in the sea and a trail in mighty waters"</span> <span class="source">(Isaiah 43:16)</span>. For this verse is the secret of the <span class="key-term">kavanos</span> [mystical intentions] of Elul, as is brought.</p>
<p>And the simple intention that emerges from this for all simple people is that Hashem <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>, in His mercy, has made known to us through His true tzadikim that <span class="scripture">"He makes a path in the sea"</span> etc. That is, even within the depths of the very great seas that sweep over the person like the roaring waves of the sea itself, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">"all Your breakers and waves have passed over me"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 42:8)</span>, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">"and You cast me into the depths, into the heart of the seas"</span> <span class="source">(Jonah 2:4)</span>, in the aspect of <span class="scripture">"You placed me in the lowest pit, in darkness, in the depths"</span> <span class="source">(Psalms 88:7)</span> — and likewise in many verses — all the more so, as a person knows within himself what he has gone through and to where he has descended and been cast through his deeds. Nevertheless, even there, there is always a path and a trail to return to Him, <span class="key-term">Yisborach</span>.</p>
<p>And the essential path is made through the aforementioned aspect — through knowing and believing that <span class="scripture">"His sovereignty rules over all,"</span> as above — in the aspect of <span class="scripture">"If I ascend to the heavens, You are there; and if I make my bed in the abyss, behold, You are there."</span> And this is the secret of the intention of Elul, the aspect of the aforementioned path that every person can merit, in whatever place he is — especially in Elul — if he believes in all of this in truth and in simplicity, as above.</p>
